;;; `open` written as a nested fact's relation in a query's claim loads, as a
;;; relation — regression `claim-fact-head`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The claim `(model (p (open k)))` lists a `p` whose value is a fact of the
;;; relation `open`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as a nested fact's relation in a query's claim, so the program
;;; loads, and every command answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, R is 4 states, and `ein solve`
;;; refutes the claim, *the claim lists 1 class, the query has 2*, exit 1; `ein
;;; saturate` and the views answer, exit 0.
;;; The engine loads it.
;;;

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(query :goal (p ?x) :expect (model (p (open k))))
